{"id":"67a70fa38edcc474","group":"93","path":"93/93-ex-profinite-groups.md","title":"Finite Discrete Profinite Group","display":"Finite Discrete Profinite Group","type":"example","metadata":{"type":"example","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-ex-profinite-groups","aliases":["93-ex-profinite-groups"],"display":"Finite Discrete Profinite Group","authors":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi","book_title":"Algebraizable Logics","depends_on":["[[93-df-profinite]]","[[93-df-group]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"example"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-ex-profinite-groups"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-ex-profinite-groups</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Finite Discrete Profinite Group"},{"key":"authors","html":"W. J. Blok, Don Pigozzi"},{"key":"book_title","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2f5dec406c92aa2e\" href=\"?note=2f5dec406c92aa2e\" title=\"93-df-profinite\">93-df-profinite</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"eb9dce8251e2dc37\" href=\"?note=eb9dce8251e2dc37\" title=\"93-df-group\">93-df-group</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"ex-profinite-groups---Finite-Discrete-Profinite-Group\">ex-profinite-groups - Finite Discrete Profinite Group</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_2\">\\(C_2\\)</span>, the multiplication, inverse, and identity-operation graphs <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m_2,q_2,e_2\">\\(m_2,q_2,e_2\\)</span>, the operation family <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\">\\(\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\\)</span>, the group <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf G_2\">\\(\\mathbf G_2\\)</span>, and its discrete topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal T_2\">\\(\\mathcal T_2\\)</span> are defined below.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S_G\">\\(S_G\\)</span>, the unary symbol <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{inv}\">\\(\\operatorname{inv}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_G\">\\(\\tau_G\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_{93}\\)</span> are sourced from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"eb9dce8251e2dc37\" href=\"?note=eb9dce8251e2dc37\" title=\"93-df-group\">93-df-group</a>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}\\)</span> is the explicit inverse-limit predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2f5dec406c92aa2e\" href=\"?note=2f5dec406c92aa2e\" title=\"93-df-profinite\">93-df-profinite</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\nC_2\\coloneqq\\{0,1\\},\n\\qquad\nm_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle\\langle0,0\\rangle,0\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle0,1\\rangle,1\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle1,0\\rangle,1\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle1,1\\rangle,0\\rangle\\},\n\\qquad\nq_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle0,0\\rangle,\\langle1,1\\rangle\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\nC_2\\coloneqq\\{0,1\\},\n\\qquad\nm_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle\\langle0,0\\rangle,0\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle0,1\\rangle,1\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle1,0\\rangle,1\\rangle,\n\\langle\\langle1,1\\rangle,0\\rangle\\},\n\\qquad\nq_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle0,0\\rangle,\\langle1,1\\rangle\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\ne_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle\\varnothing,0\\rangle\\},\\qquad\n\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\\coloneqq\n\\{\\langle\\cdot,m_2\\rangle,\\langle\\operatorname{inv},q_2\\rangle,\n\\langle e,e_2\\rangle\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\ne_2\\coloneqq\\{\\langle\\varnothing,0\\rangle\\},\\qquad\n\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\\coloneqq\n\\{\\langle\\cdot,m_2\\rangle,\\langle\\operatorname{inv},q_2\\rangle,\n\\langle e,e_2\\rangle\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\n\\mathbf G_2\\coloneqq\n\\langle C_2,\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\\rangle,\n\\qquad\\mathcal T_2\\coloneqq\\mathcal P(C_2)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\n\\mathbf G_2\\coloneqq\n\\langle C_2,\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}\\rangle,\n\\qquad\\mathcal T_2\\coloneqq\\mathcal P(C_2)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\nm_2:C_2^2\\to C_2\n\\land q_2:C_2\\to C_2\n\\land e_2:C_2^0\\to C_2\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_{93}(\\mathbf G_2)\n\\land\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}(\\langle\\mathbf G_2,\\mathcal T_2\\rangle;\\tau_G).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ex\\text{-}profinite\\text{-}groups}\\vdash\nm_2:C_2^2\\to C_2\n\\land q_2:C_2\\to C_2\n\\land e_2:C_2^0\\to C_2\n\\land\\mathrm{Group}_{93}(\\mathbf G_2)\n\\land\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}(\\langle\\mathbf G_2,\\mathcal T_2\\rangle;\\tau_G).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The cyclic group of order two with the discrete topology is a constant\ninverse limit of a finite discrete group and hence profinite. Every basic\noperation, including the nullary identity, is an explicit graph; no Galois\nor Krull-topology infrastructure is left implicit.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"ex-profinite-groups---Finite-Discrete-Profinite-Group","text":"ex-profinite-groups - Finite Discrete Profinite Group","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-profinite","status":"resolved","id":"2f5dec406c92aa2e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-profinite]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-group","status":"resolved","id":"eb9dce8251e2dc37","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-group","status":"resolved","id":"eb9dce8251e2dc37","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$S_G$, the unary symbol $\\operatorname{inv}$, $\\tau_G$, and $\\mathrm{Group}_{93}$ are sourced from [[93-df-group]], and $\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}$ is the explicit inverse-limit predicate of [[93-df-profinite]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-profinite","status":"resolved","id":"2f5dec406c92aa2e","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$S_G$, the unary symbol $\\operatorname{inv}$, $\\tau_G$, and $\\mathrm{Group}_{93}$ are sourced from [[93-df-group]], and $\\mathrm{Profinite}_{93}$ is the explicit inverse-limit predicate of [[93-df-profinite]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"C_2","display":false},{"tex":"m_2,q_2,e_2","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{G2OpFam}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf G_2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal T_2","display":false},{"tex":"S_G","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{inv}","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_G","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{G